From f1a244f29ae6ae08d46eb78412c99c7232be5748 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: CipherScope <dev@cipherscope.io>
Date: Mon, 5 Oct 2026 22:31:58 -0600
Subject: [PATCH 56/65] consensus: deploy P2MR leaf version 0xe0 with tripwire
 outputs

A buried deployment, p2mr_tripwire, sets SCRIPT_VERIFY_P2MR_TRIPWIRE on
blocks at or above its height where P2MR is active too, so that P2MR leaves
of leaf version 0xe0 execute there. Next to its height, P2MRTripwireHeight,
the consensus parameters gain the tripwire outputs, p2mr_tripwires: from
that height on, validation is to fail elliptic curve checks in those leaves
in every block whose parent leaves one of them missing, which a later commit
in this series implements. An output is present while it is unspent and was
created below the height.

- On the Ark-0 signet the height and the outputs are rules of that network,
  ARK0_TRIPWIRE_HEIGHT and ARK0_TRIPWIRE_OUTPOINTS, each output with the
  x-only key its leaf checks and a label. Neither is set yet: the height is
  std::numeric_limits<int>::max() and the list is empty, so this build does
  not activate the rules on Ark-0. A commit of its own sets both, once the
  two outputs are confirmed below the height. A static_assert keeps the
  height above ARK0_MLDSA44_HEIGHT.
- Another custom signet gets the rules only from
  -signettripwire=<height>@<txid:vout>[,<txid:vout>...], and since leaf
  version 0xe0 runs OP_CHECKMLDSA44, which only Ark-0 activated so far, the
  new -signetmldsa44=<height> activates that opcode on such a signet. The
  tripwire option requires -signetmldsa44 below its height; both require
  -signetchallenge, and Ark-0 refuses both.
- Regtest activates leaf version 0xe0 at genesis without tripwire outputs,
  unless -testactivationheight=p2mr_tripwire@N moves it. -signettripwire
  works there too and then sets the height, which must be above that of
  p2mr_mldsa44, and not also be given by -testactivationheight.
- Mainnet, testnet3, testnet4 and the default signet never activate it.
  A node refuses to start with either option on a chain it is not for,
  whatever its value, rather than ignore it: -signetmldsa44 is only for
  signets, -signettripwire for signets and regtest.

getdeploymentinfo reports the deployment, and a signet or regtest node with
tripwire outputs logs the height and the outputs at startup: the outpoints,
and for those the code fixes their label and, unless it is the BIP-341 NUMS
point, the SHA256 of their key.
